- The handler refuses an absent body: read at `index.ts:440`-`:457` at the tip (`updateTenantSchema.parse(req.body)` `:442`; `if (sets.length === 0)` -> 400 "No fields to update" `:455`-`:457`; `express.json` `:19`). A replica probe (express 4.22.2 + `express.json()`, the schema and the gate byte-copied from `:431`-`:457`, scratch only) answered 400 "No fields to update" for no body, for a zero-length JSON body and for `{}`; its positive control (a schema with a required field) answered 400 too, and the referral generate gate in the same probe answered 201, so the probe can tell a refusal from an acceptance.
